      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Drive on a rolling physical flatbed; your truck's weight and wheel forces
    affect it. Movement controls steer/balance, ACTION hops when your actual wheels
    contact the deck, with a short recovery between hops. Freestyle banks clean airborne
    landings, rotations, balance and ride distance. Longest Ride scores only supported
    riding time plus airborne time that ends back on the deck. Ramp Attack scores
    the trailer's genuine ramp takeoffs and landings while you remain aboard, not
    ordinary truck hops. Trick Challenge banks landed quarter-turns of at least 90
    degrees, with clean-landing combos. Falling off ends your ride. The trailer gets
    one starting impulse; slopes, collisions and your weight determine the rest.
    No invisible joint attaches the truck to the deck.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
